      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVIII. Ciricsceattas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.12"/> sín agifene be sc̄e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.13"/> Martines mæssan; gif hwa ðæt ne gelæste, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.2-2"/> he scyldig LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.14"/> scill. ⁊ be XIIfealdum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.15"/> agife þone ciricsceat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVIII. Ciricsceattas sien agifene be sce. Martines mæssan; gif hwa þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne gelæste, sie he scildig LX scill' ⁊ be XIIfealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> agife ðone ciricsceat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVIII. Ciricsceattas syn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.1"/> agifene be sc̄e Martines mæssan; gif hwa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.8-2"/> þæt ne gelæste, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.1"/> he scyldig LX scll' ⁊ be XIIfealdum agife ðone ciricsceat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.9-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ciricsceatte. Cyricsceattas syn ageuene be sc̄e Martynes mæssan; gyf hwa þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>læste, sy he scyldig feortig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.2"/> scill' ⁊ be twelffealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> agyfe ðone cyricsceat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Ciricsceattas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.7"/> reddita sint in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.8"/> festo sancti Martini; si quis hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.9"/> non compleat, reus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.10"/> sit LX sol. et duodecuplo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_4.lnote.oe.11"/> reddat ipsum cyricsceattum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="36" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ciricsceatte<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_4.attnote.fn.11"/>.] Ciricsceattas sín agifene be scē. Martines mæssan; gif hwa ðæt ne gelæste, sie he scyldig LX<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_4.attnote.fn.12"/> scill. ⁊ be XII fealdum agife þone ciricsceat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="4" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="374" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>(XLVIII} Ciricsceattas sin agifene be s<hi rend="italic">anc</hi>te Martines mæssan; gif hwa ðæt ne gelæste, sie he scyldig LX sciƚƚ ⁊ be XIIfealdum agife þone ciricsceat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Kirchensteuern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_4.lnote.de.1"/> seien zur Sanct Martins-Messe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_4.lnote.de.2"/> abgegeben; wenn jemand dies nicht leistet, sei er 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_4.lnote.de.3"/> Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_4.lnote.de.4"/> [dem König] schuldig und gebe 12fach<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_4.lnote.de.5"/> den Kirchenschoss [der Kirche] ab.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Let church dues be paid by Martinmas; if anyone does not pay them, let him be liable for 60 shillings [to the king] and pay the church due 12-fold [to the church].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="37" ed="#attenborough"/>Church dues shall be rendered at Martinmas. If anyone fails to do so, he shall forfeit 60 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_4.attnote.n.1"/> and render 12 times the church dues<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_4.attnote.n.2"/> [in addition].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="400" ed="#whitelock"/>Church-scot is to be given by Martinmas; if anyone does not discharge it, he is to be liable to 60 shillings and to render the church-scot twelve-fold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="375" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Church dues are to be given by St. Martin’s Mass; if someone neglects this, let him be liable for [a fine of] 60 shillings and let him render the church dues twelve-fold.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIEg_3">II Eg 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="375"><label>matches</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_1">Abt 1</ref> <quote>The latter payment matches the twelve-fold restitution for theft from a church established in Æthelberht §1.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="375"><label>see also</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_61">Ine 61</ref> <quote>See also §65.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="423"><ref target="clause:Ine_61">Ine 61</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="28"><ref target="clause:IIEg_2-2">II Eg 2.2–3</ref></note>
